    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "olh3kc8",
      "content": "Child Health Nursing (Pediatric Nursing) focuses on the health care of infants, children, and adolescents. It includes growth and development monitoring, nutrition, immunization, prevention of childhood diseases, and nursing care for sick children. In nursing competitive exams such as RRB Nursing, common questions come from growth milestones, immunization schedules, common pediatric diseases, and neonatal care."
    },
